        "abstract": "We consider the subject of conduction and breakdown in vacuum in two parts. The first, under the title Vacuum Breakdown, deals with transitional phenomena by which a normally insulating vacuum gap becomes an electrical conductor. The second is entitled Vacuum Arcs and is concerned with the longer term effects which allow the space between two electrodes in an evacuated chamber to carry large currents with a relatively small total voltage drop.",
