        "abstract": "Most of the fundamental problems of condensed matter physics require experimental investigation at low temperatures. Typically, dielectric studies are one technique among many employed simultaneously to investigate a particular physical problem or a particular insulating material, so that the distinction between dielectric and other properties is often artificial and unhelpful. In some areas we have included non-dielectric publications as we find these essential to an understanding of the topic (e.g. glasses) and other areas we have banned entirely from the text, as the topics are too specialised and too voluminous (e.g. quasi-one-dimensional systems). We have not attempted to touch upon excitonic phenomena.",
